---
/** About the data: sources, definitions, years, the six locale groups, and the unmapped entities. */
import { TIER_DEFINITIONS, UNMAPPED, districts } from '../../lib/gapmap';
---

<section class="gm-section gm-about" aria-labelledby="gm-about-heading">
  <div class="gm-section__head">
    <h2 id="gm-about-heading" class="gm-section__title">About the data</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="gm-about__body">
    <h3>Sources</h3>
    <p>
      Librarian and teacher staffing: Office of Superintendent of Public Instruction (OSPI), SLIDE staffing data, 2015–16
      through 2024–25. Reading results: OSPI Report Card, Smarter Balanced English language arts assessment, including
      OSPI’s statewide figures. Locale groups: U.S. Department of Education, National Center for Education Statistics
      (NCES), Elementary/Secondary Information System (ELSI) locale codes. District boundaries: OSPI, via the Washington
      Geospatial Open Data Portal (geo.wa.gov), simplified for the web.
    </p>

    <h3>What counts as having a librarian</h3>
    <p>
      Staffing is measured in full-time-equivalent (FTE) positions reported by each district. A district “has a
      librarian” if it reported more than zero librarian FTE for the school year; it has “at least one full-time
      librarian” at 1.0 FTE or more. Where a district reported no librarian FTE, ratios such as students per librarian
      don’t apply and are shown as a dash.
    </p>

    <h3>Years covered</h3>
    <p>
      Staffing data covers the 2015–16 through 2024–25 school years. Reading results are shown for 2024–25 only. Statewide
      testing did not take place in 2019–20 because of COVID-19.
    </p>

    <h3>Locale groups</h3>
    <p>
      Each district is placed in one of six groups based on its NCES locale code for that school year. A district’s
      group can change from year to year when NCES updates its classifications.
    </p>
    <div class="gm-table-scroll">
      <table class="gm-about__tiers">
        <caption class="visually-hidden">The six locale groups and the NCES locale categories in each</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Group</th>
            <th scope="col">NCES locale categories (codes)</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            TIER_DEFINITIONS.map((t) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">{t.tier}</th>
                <td>{t.nces}</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      “Mid-size” corresponds to NCES’s Town category. Large Urban consists solely of Seattle Public Schools, the only
      Washington district in NCES’s large-city category. It is shown as its own group because, with its very large number
      of schools, combining it with other city districts would distort the comparison.
    </p>

    <h3>Entities without a map shape</h3>
    <p>
      The data includes {districts.length} districts and entities. {UNMAPPED.length} of them have no map shape because they
      are not geographic school districts: {UNMAPPED.join(', ')}. They are included in the search and the table. The
      Washington State Center for Childhood Deafness and Hearing Loss has no NCES locale code, so it has no locale group.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .gm-about__body {
    max-width: var(--prose-width);
  }
  .gm-about__body h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    margin: var(--space-6) 0 var(--space-2);
  }
  .gm-about__body h3:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .gm-about__body p {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
  }
  .gm-about__tiers {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }
</style>
